From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000027 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Li Yiming <liyiming@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm: fsl-imx6ul: Program the generic timer at 8 MHz

The i.MX6UL/6ULL system counter runs at 8 MHz.  U-Boot's syscounter
driver programmes CNTFRQ with that rate (CFG_SC_TIMER_CLK) and converts
every tick to microseconds using the value read back from CNTFRQ.

QEMU implements CNTFRQ as reads-as-written while the counter itself
advances at cpu->gt_cntfrq_hz.  For Cortex-A7 that is the backwards
compatible 62.5 MHz, so the value U-Boot reads back (8 MHz) does not
match the rate the counter actually ticks at.  The resulting timebase
runs 7.8x fast: U-Boot reports "9260808 bytes read in 15883 ms" for a
2 second transfer, cyclic callbacks trip their watchdog thresholds and
the boot delay elapses eight times too quickly.

Set the CPU "cntfrq" property before realize so the counter and the
value the guest reads agree, as they do on the real SoC.

Signed-off-by: Li Yiming <liyiming@localhost>
---
 hw/arm/fsl-imx6ul.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/arm/fsl-imx6ul.c b/hw/arm/fsl-imx6ul.c
--- a/hw/arm/fsl-imx6ul.c
+++ b/hw/arm/fsl-imx6ul.c
@@ -244,6 +244,13 @@
         return;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * The i.MX system counter runs at 8 MHz.  U-Boot programs CNTFRQ with
+     * that rate and derives every timeout from it, so the CPU's generic
+     * timer must tick at the same frequency instead of QEMU's default.
+     */
+    qdev_prop_set_uint64(DEVICE(&s->cpu), "cntfrq", 8000000);
+
     qdev_realize(DEVICE(&s->cpu), NULL, &error_abort);
 
     /*
